From 590d8d33c32e5dd28d921ce78e719ebc49e229a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:19:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(color): ICC image descriptions and icc_file
 advertising

Characterized output and preferred descriptions report the panel's custom
primaries and must send `icc_file`: exact bytes for a configured profile,
a synthesized matrix-shaper profile for EDID characterization. Clients
may build descriptions from their own ICC files via `create_icc`
(features `icc_v2_v4` and `set_tf_power`): ICC v2/v4, Display or
ColorSpace class, matrix-shaper only, <=32 MB; bad profiles arrive as
`failed`/`information_allowed=false`, never as protocol errors beyond the
contract's four. Client-created descriptions deny `get_information` per
the create contract. Non-representable TRCs are power-fit and rendered as
the nearest named curve (per-buffer 3D LUTs are a follow-up).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
