A gamma-control ramp composed after a baked panel-TRC curve produced two
3x1D LUT stages, which the renderer's collector rejects — output frames
failed for as long as Night Light ran with a panel TRC that matched no
named curve. Consecutive LUTs now fold into one table at compose time.
